omy moving forward.]  [At White House, Council of Economic Advisers chairman Gregory MANKIW&#134;- defends the economy.]  Statement from White House chief of staff Andrew Card quoted.  [On Wednesday, BUSH, KERRY&nbsp- offer views on \"turning the corner.\"]  Kerry's suggestions for creating new jobs outlined on screen.  [American Enterprise Inst. Kevin HASSETT&#134;- says the economy could be bad news for Bush.]", "segment_duration": 270, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761649, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "e8SqBbg65n", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-06", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761648, "segment_id": "z0wPHLswBC", "segment_broadcast_id": "e8SqBbg65n", "segment_title": "Iraq / Revolt / Sadr City", "segment_description": "(Studio: Elizabeth Vargas)  Report introduced. \n (Baghdad: Mike Lee)  An uprising in Iraq by insurgent militias loyal to Shiite cleric Muqtada al-Sadr featured; scenes shown from Najaf, Basra & Baghdad's Sadr City.  [11th Marine Expeditionary Unit commander Col. Anthony HASLAM&#134;- outlines the mission to clean the militia out of the cemetery.]  The sudden flight of moderate Shiite leader Ayatollah Ali Sistani out of the country with heart problems noted. \n (Studio: Elizabeth Vargas)  Report introduced. \n (Sadr City: Martha Raddatz)  The low-level war that has been fought by the US in Sadr City featured; scenes shown from this poor part of Baghdad.  [ABC News military analyst Tony CORDESMAN&#134;- says al-Sadr has been underestimated as a political force.]  [1st Cavalry Div. Lt. Col. Gary VOLESKY&#134;- talks to the citizens.]", "segment_duration": 220, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63320.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761650, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "e8SqBbg65n", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-06", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761648, "segment_id": "OwknICZTZc", "segment_broadcast_id": "e8SqBbg65n", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items (Studio: Elizabeth Vargas)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 20, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63540.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761651, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "e8SqBbg65n", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-06", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761648, "segment_id": "0Smx3UzeBM", "segment_broadcast_id": "e8SqBbg65n", "segment_title": "(Commercial: Big Lots; Bush's Baked Beans; Accu-Chek; Minute Maid; Bayer; Cheerios.)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 3, "segment_start_time": "63560.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761652, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Commercial", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "e8SqBbg65n", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-0